# Backshelf - the Gemini key, option A of two.
#
# OPTION B, and the easier one: open the running app and paste the key into the
# byLLM panel in the left rail, then press SAVE KEY. It lands on an LlmConfig
# node in the graph, takes effect on the very next scan with no restart and no
# redeploy, survives a restart, and an empty key clears it back to MockLLM.
# That path works on Railway too, where this file does not exist. See
# settings.sv.jac. A key stored in the graph WINS over the variable below.
#
# Option A is this file, and it is still the right one for a machine you own:
#
#   cp .env.example .env        # then paste the real key on the GEMINI_API_KEY line
#   ./.venv/bin/jac start main.jac
#
# That is the whole procedure. There is no second step, no `export`, and no
# other file to edit. `jac start` reads this .env by itself: byLLM imports
# litellm, and litellm calls load_dotenv() at import time, which walks up from
# .venv/lib/.../site-packages/litellm to the repo root and finds this file.
#
# Verified by execution. With only .env on disk and GEMINI_API_KEY absent from
# the shell environment, IntakeScan reached generativelanguage.googleapis.com
# and failed on the dummy key. Deleting .env put the same call back on the
# MockLLM fallback (using_mock_llm: true).
#
# The switch is `LlmRouter` in llm.sv.jac, resolved on every call:
#   key on the LlmConfig node -> real Gemini, no restart          (option B)
#   GEMINI_API_KEY set        -> real Gemini through byLLM        (option A)
#   neither                   -> DemoLLM (a MockLLM), app still runs
#
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# .env is gitignored. Never commit the real key.

GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Any litellm model id. Defaults to gemini/gemini-2.0-flash.
# BACKSHELF_MODEL=gemini/gemini-2.0-flash


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployed (Railway / any container): .env does NOT work here, use a real var
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# In the Dockerfile the venv is /opt/venv while the code is /app, so litellm's
# load_dotenv() walks up from /opt/venv and never reaches /app/.env. On top of
# that .env is gitignored and dockerignored, so it is not in the image at all.
#
# On Railway, either set GEMINI_API_KEY in the service Variables tab (nothing
# in the code changes - os.getenv finds it either way, but the service has to
# restart), or just paste the key into the deployed app's byLLM panel, which
# needs neither a variable nor a restart.
